# The one shared UBSan suppression file (rule R5).
#
# Rule R5:
#   - Each build uses -fsanitize=undefined -fno-sanitize-recover=undefined.
#     The first report stops the run.
#   - Only a check with a known, tracked finding can recover, with
#     -fsanitize-recover=<that check> and the runtime option halt_on_error=1.
#     tests/sanitizers/ubsan.cmake gives these flags.
#   - An entry of this file has an effect only for such a recoverable check.
#   - Each entry names one function. Never a file, never a src: wildcard.
#   - Each entry has a comment with its reason, its evidence, its task
#     number and its date.
#
# Each pattern is anchored. The sanitizer runtime matches a pattern as a
# substring of the function name (TemplateMatch of sanitizer_common), thus
# "function:ggml_compute_forward_mul_mat" also matches
# ggml_compute_forward_mul_mat_one_chunk, _id and _id_one_chunk. The
# reproducer showed this on 2026-09-23. Thus:
#   - A C function: ^name$.
#   - A C++ function: ^name( (the symbolizer adds the parameter types).
#   - A C++ function template: name< (the symbolizer puts the return type
#     first, for example "void ggml_compute_forward_set_rows_impl<float, long>(...)").
#
# Rule R13: tests/sanitizers/supp-repro.sh runs the reproducer of each entry
# (tests/sanitizers/repro/ubsan_ggml.c) in the debug and the release profile.
# An entry that matches in one profile only has the marker
# "R13: <profile> only" in its comment.
#
# tests/sanitizers/env.sh gives this file to UBSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=.

# Task #156, 2026-09-23. The supports_op of MUL_MAT_ID (ggml-hexagon.cpp:5122 in
# ggml_hexagon_precompute_matmul_params_impl, and 5438 in ggml_hexagon_precompute_fused_mmnx_params)
# calls init_fastdiv_values(ne12 / ne02). With fewer tokens than experts the argument is 0, and
# hex-fastdiv.h:22 divides by zero. Found by the phone probe of fuzz-hexhost. fuzz-hexhost owns the
# fix. Remove this entry when task #156 lands.
# Evidence (supp-repro.sh, regress/kparams/mm-id-div-zero.bin of hexhost, clang 22.1.8): the report
# frames are "#0 init_fastdiv_values(unsigned int)" and "#1 ggml_hexagon_precompute_matmul_params_impl"
# at one PC. Here the runtime matches the inlined frame #0: "^ggml_hexagon_precompute_matmul_params_impl("
# does not match, "init_fastdiv_values" matches. Thus the entry covers each d = 0 of
# init_fastdiv_values, from each caller. On x86 the division traps with SIGFPE after the suppressed
# report. On arm64 it gives 0 and the run continues.
integer-divide-by-zero:^init_fastdiv_values(
